
See: https://claude.ai/share/f6184279-bff5-491a-a659-c0d3aef14fe8

Image 1: models-base (built rarely)
dockerfileFROM nvidia/cuda:12.x-runtime-ubuntu22.04

COPY --link models/model_a/ /app/models/model_a/
COPY --link models/model_b/ /app/models/model_b/
COPY --link models/model_c/ /app/models/model_c/


Image 2: comfyui-app (built frequently)
dockerfileFROM models-base AS models

FROM nvidia/cuda:12.x-runtime-ubuntu22.04

# System + Python deps
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y ...
COPY requirements.txt /app/
RUN pip install -r /app/requirements.txt

# ComfyUI
COPY comfyui/ /app/comfyui/

# Pull models from the stable image — layers keep their hash
COPY --from=models /app/models/ /app/models/

COPY scripts/ /app/scripts/
ENTRYPOINT ["/app/scripts/start.sh"]



The critical detail for hash preservation: COPY --from with --link is what you
want here. Without --link, the layer hash depends on the layers below it (the
parent chain), so any change to your apt-get or pip layers would produce a new
hash for the model layers even though the content is identical. With --link:

dockerfile
COPY --link --from=models /app/models/model_a/ /app/models/model_a/
COPY --link --from=models /app/models/model_b/ /app/models/model_b/
COPY --link --from=models /app/models/model_c/ /app/models/model_c/


Each model layer's digest is purely a function of its content. Change your pip
requirements, rebuild, push — the registry already has those model blobs, push
skips them entirely.

One thing to watch out for: make sure you're referencing models-base by digest
in production builds, not just a mutable tag:

dockerfile
FROM us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/your-project/repo/models-base@sha256:abc123... AS models

If you reference by tag and someone rebuilds models-base with identical content
but a different BuildKit version or timestamp metadata, you could end up with
different layer hashes unexpectedly. Pinning by digest guarantees reproducibility.

Workflow then becomes:

Models change → rebuild and push models-base (slow, but rare), update the digest reference
App code changes → rebuild comfyui-app (fast, only small layers are new), push is quick
since model layers already exist in the registry

This should make your crane pushes much more pleasant — you'll only be pushing the small
delta layers on routine builds instead of re-uploading those big blobs every time.
